@page "/privacy"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<div class="legal-container">
    <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: November 14, 2026</p>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <p>
            RSS Reader is a free and <a href="https://github.com/brandonchastain/rss-reader">open source</a>
            reader for RSS and Atom feeds that focuses on privacy &amp; functionality.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>What's stored</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>An account ID from Microsoft, Google or GitHub, so you can sign in. Never your name or email.</li>
            <li>Your feeds, tags, and which articles you've read or saved.</li>
            <li>Error logs, without IP addresses, deleted after 30 days.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            There are no ads, no analytics and no tracking, and your data is never sold. It's encrypted and
            hosted on Microsoft Azure in the US.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Signing in and cookies</h2>
        <p>
            When you sign in, Microsoft, Google or GitHub shares your email address with RSS Reader. It's kept
            only inside an encrypted sign-in cookie in your browser, to keep you signed in, and is never saved
            on the server. That's the only cookie. Your browser also keeps your settings and a copy of your
            feed so the app loads quickly.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Who else is involved</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Microsoft, Google or GitHub, whichever you sign in with, handles your sign-in and password.</li>
            <li>Microsoft Azure hosts the app and its data.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Your data isn't shared with anyone else unless the law requires it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Your data</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>See it:</strong> &ldquo;View My Data&rdquo; on the <a href="/account">Account page</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Export your feeds:</strong> OPML export on the <a href="/feeds">Feeds page</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Change it:</strong> edit your feeds and tags anytime in the app.</li>
            <li>
                <strong>Delete it:</strong> &ldquo;Delete My Account&rdquo; on the <a href="/account">Account page</a>
                deletes your data right away. Backups may keep a copy for a while.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Law enforcement requests</h2>
        <p>
            As of November 14, 2026, RSS Reader has never received a subpoena, court order, warrant, national
            security letter or any other government request for user data, and has never been placed under a gag
            order. This statement is updated every three months. If it hasn't been updated by February 14, 2027,
            or it disappears, assume it's no longer true.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
        <p>RSS Reader doesn't track you, so browser Do Not Track settings don't change anything.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>RSS Reader isn't meant for children under 13.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>Changes to this policy will be posted on this page with a new date.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>Open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/brandonchastain/rss-reader/issues">GitHub</a>.</p>
    </section>
</div>
